<title>UK: Whessoe unit wins $4.6 mln U.S. deal.</title>
<headline>Whessoe unit wins $4.6 mln U.S. deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Whessoe Plc said on Thursday that its U.S. subsidiary Coggins Systems had won an order from the United States Department of Defence valued at $4.6 million.</p>
<p>In a statement, the group said the deal concerned deployment of its real time fuels management system.</p>
<p>This contract follows a software deal that Coggins had bagged from U.S. defence valued at five million dollars in September 1996.</p>
<p>According to the new deal, Coggins would have to deploy its fuel management system at 600 fuel storage locations.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
